    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40396" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rāpīcĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		rapum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to rapes</i> or <i>turnips</i>, <i>rape-</i>, <i>turnip-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 35, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">semen,</span>”
				<i>rape-seed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 134, 1</span></i>
			.— As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rāpīcĭi</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m. (sc. caules), <i>turnip-shoots</i>, <i>young
				turnipplants</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 13, 34, §
		127</span></i>.</div>
